# You do NOT need this file for normal setup anymore. Run printer-agent.exe and it will
# auto-detect your printer (if it's the only one installed) or open a setup page in your browser
# to pick it — nothing to copy or edit. That choice is saved automatically under
# %LOCALAPPDATA%\SeaErpPrintAgent\config.json.
#
# This file is only for advanced/dev overrides: copy it to .env next to the exe (or in this
# source folder) and any value set here wins over both auto-detection and the setup page.

# The exact name of the printer as Windows knows it (Control Panel > Devices and Printers,
# or run `Get-Printer` in PowerShell).
PRINTER_NAME="TSC TTP-244 Pro"

# Port the agent listens on, loopback-only (127.0.0.1). Change only if 9101 conflicts with
# something else already running on this PC.
PRINT_AGENT_PORT=9101

# Origin(s) the web app is served from, so the browser's CORS preflight succeeds. "*" is fine
# for v1 since the agent only ever listens on 127.0.0.1 regardless of this setting — narrow it
# if that assumption ever changes.
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=*

# How a label reaches the printer. "driver" (default) draws the tag and prints it through the
# Windows driver, like any Windows program — this is what the TTP-244 Pro needs. "raw" sends TSPL
# straight to the port monitor, which locked that printer up; only use it for a different printer.
# PRINT_MODE=driver
